00:21:00,520 --> 00:21:02,520
reproachfully to Mrs.

228
00:21:02,520 --> 00:21:09,119
Medlock. "Oh, sir," she panted. "I don't know how it's happened. There's not a servant

229
00:21:09,119 --> 00:21:14,000
on the place that dare to talk— —they all have their orders."

230
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:20,199
"Nobody told her anything," said Colin, "she heard me crying and found me herself. I

231
00:21:20,199 --> 00:21:26,158
am glad she came. Don't be silly, Medlock." Mary saw that Dr. Craven did not

232
00:21:26,158 --> 00:21:31,879
look pleased, but it was quite plain that he dare not oppose his patient. He sat

233
00:21:31,879 --> 00:21:37,879
down by Colin and felt his pulse I'm afraid there has been too much

