00:22:18,559 --> 00:22:22,119
room." "She came into the room last night.

242
00:22:22,119 --> 00:22:27,478
She stayed with me a long time. She sang a Hindustani song to me and it made me

243
00:22:27,478 --> 00:22:33,079
go to sleep," said Colin. "I was better when I wakened up. I wanted my breakfast. I

244
00:22:33,079 --> 00:22:41,318
want my tea now. Tell nurse, Medlock Dr. Craven did not stay very long.

245
00:22:41,318 --> 00:22:44,760
He talked to the nurse for a few minutes when she came came into the room and

246
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:50,439
said a few words of warning to Colin. He must not talk too much; he must

247
00:22:50,439 --> 00:22:54,840
not forget that he was ill; he must not forget that he was very easily

248
00:22:54,840 --> 00:23:01,439
tired. Mary thought that there seemed to be a number of uncomfortable things he was not to

249
00:23:01,439 --> 00:23:07,959
forget. Colin looked fretful and kept his strange black lashed eyes fixed on Dr.

250
00:23:07,959 --> 00:23:15,680
Craven's face. "I want to forget it," he said at last. "She makes me forget it. That

251
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:19,639
is why I want her." Dr. Craven did not look

252
00:23:19,639 --> 00:23:23,799
happy when he left the room. He gave a puzzled glance at the little girl

253
00:23:23,799 --> 00:23:28,600
sitting on the large stool. She had become a stiff, silent child again as

